From: usdtweak <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] x11: initialize warpCursorPos sentinel on window creation

The X11 path already implements the warpCursorPos guard pattern that
patch 0002 ports to Win32.  This patch is a small audit fix: the
warpCursorPosX/Y fields are zero-initialized via calloc, which
coincides with the valid coordinate (0, 0).  If the user happens to
move the cursor to the window's top-left pixel before any
_glfwSetCursorPosX11 call has occurred, the MotionNotify warp guard
would falsely match and silently swallow the event.

In practice this is rare and benign (the next motion event would
re-establish the position), but for parity with the Win32 fix in
patch 0002 and as a defensive correctness improvement, we initialize
both fields to INT_MIN explicitly in _glfwCreateWindowX11.

--- a/src/x11_window.c
+++ b/src/x11_window.c
@@ -1964,6 +1964,13 @@
     Visual* visual = NULL;
     int depth;

+    // Sentinel: no warp pending.  Avoids a false positive in the
+    // MotionNotify warp guard if the user happens to move the cursor to
+    // (0, 0) before any _glfwSetCursorPosX11 call (calloc-zero would
+    // otherwise coincide with the valid coordinate (0, 0)).
+    window->x11.warpCursorPosX = INT_MIN;
+    window->x11.warpCursorPosY = INT_MIN;
+
     if (ctxconfig->client != GLFW_NO_API)
     {
         if (ctxconfig->source == GLFW_NATIVE_CONTEXT_API)
